WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
Every year, statisticians
measure the size of their economy

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.750
in three separate ways.

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.670
They add up the value
of everything produced.

4
00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.950
They add up every income earned.

5
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.270
They add up everything spent.

6
00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:15.560
Yet the three totals come out the same,

7
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.920
apart from small measurement errors.

8
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.950
Why must a country's total spending,

9
00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:24.160
total income and total
output always be equal?

10
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.990
In this mission, you'll
follow money and goods around

11
00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:29.980
a simple economy of households and firms.

12
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.510
Then you'll see what happens
when money leaks out of the flow,

13
00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.940
as it did in spring 2020.

14
00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.890
Your mission: find out why
the three totals must match.
